/// Synopsis: the documented limits of the animations when the covered part is glued to the visible one, each next to its way out where it has one: with this theme, Touying's `#item-by-item` shows every item on every step; a `#speaker-note` glued to the items shows the covered item, because Touying puts the note before the covered part and the veil of the theme gets no height there (the note after a blank line does not); a covered line glued to a visible one and followed by a shape, or by an image, shows on the first step (the `#pause` in a paragraph of its own veils it); a `#pause` and an `#uncover` in one paragraph: Touying moves the covered part, and the first step reads "First. Third. Second. Fourth." (one paragraph each keeps the order). The other documented limits are in the other `sections/pause-limits-*` tests; "Unsupported mark" in `tests/errors/`; the covered content that runs on to the next page in `sections/pause-overflow`.
#import "../../common.typ": *
#show: setup
#include "body.typ"
